              "sourceId": "kno_seedAmara1",
              "title": "Meridian Shift Fatigue Review 2025.pdf",
              "locator": "p. 6",
              "text": "Poor sleep was the most common complaint, named by 63% of respondents. Staff who slept under six hours before a shift were twice as likely to report a near-miss medication error that week.",
