              "title": "Meridian Shift Fatigue Review 2025.pdf",
              "locator": "p. 3",
              "text": "Staff working more than three consecutive long shifts reported fatigue scores 38% higher than colleagues on shorter blocks. The effect was strongest in emergency and acute medicine, where rest days were most often cancelled at short notice.",
