      },
      "content": "Nobody here is pro-burnout. My problem is the word *nationwide*. The pilots I've seen were mostly voluntary, self-selected firms, often knowledge work,[1] where output is hard to measure and easy to reorganise.[2] A hospital, a bus network or a care home can't compress five days of coverage into four. They hire more staff or they cut service. Both cost money that somebody pays.",
      "status": "complete",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-01T10:02:59.744Z",
      "emotion": "thinking",
      "emotionSource": "llm",
      "usage": {
